# Every text file is LF in every working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is structural, not stylistic. `testdata/schema/*.golden` is compared
# byte for byte against freshly generated SQL (test/integration/schema_golden_test.go),
# and Git's own default on Windows — core.autocrlf=true, which is what
# GitHub's windows-latest image ships — rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# That alone turned `integration (windows)` red on a schema nothing had
# touched: the committed golden and the generated one differed only in
# bytes no one had written.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes on commit and checks out LF everywhere, so
# a byte-comparing gate cannot be defeated by which platform cloned the
# repo. It also keeps the shell scripts under scripts/ executable by a
# POSIX shell after a round trip through a Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files Git must never touch. Listed explicitly rather than trusted
# to detection, since a false positive here corrupts the file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.wasm binary
